- dismiss_watchtower_item

Callable after find_tools:
- list_carriers — List the carriers this organization tenders freight to, narrowed by status, compliance, safety rating or authority number.
- get_carrier — Retrieve one carrier by id, including its authority, insurance and compliance state.
- create_carrier — Add a carrier the organization can tender freight to: its code, name, USDOT and MC numbers, SCAC, address and dispatch contact.
- update_carrier — Change a carrier's details: name, numbers, SCAC, address, dispatch contact, notes, or payment and remit-to details.
- update_carrier_status — Set one or more carriers Active, Inactive or DoNotUse, which decides whether they can be tendered freight.
- list_customers — List customers narrowed by status, code, name or city, with their ids.
- get_customer — Retrieve one customer by id, with their billing and email profiles.
- create_customer — Add a customer the organization ships for: its code, name, billing address and DOT and MC numbers.
- update_customer — Change a customer's details: name, billing address, DOT and MC numbers, who is emailed status updates, and consolidation.
- update_customer_status — Set one or more customers Active or Inactive, which decides whether shipments can be booked for them.
- list_commodities — List commodities — what this organization hauls, with freight class, handling flags and whether the commodity is hazardous.
- create_commodity — Add a commodity shipments can carry, with its freight class, temperature range, dimensions and handling.
- update_commodity — Change a commodity: its name, description, freight class, temperature range, dimensions, handling or hazardous material.
- update_commodity_status — Set one or more commodities Active or Inactive, which decides whether shipments can name them.
- list_hazardous_materials — List the hazardous materials this organization is set up to haul, with hazard class, UN number, packing group and whether a placard is required.
- create_hazardous_material — Add a hazardous material commodities can name, with its hazard class, UN number and packing group.
- update_hazardous_material — Change a hazardous material: its class, UN number, packing group, shipping name, placarding, handling or emergency contact.
- update_hazardous_material_status — Set one or more hazardous materials Active or Inactive, which decides whether commodities can name them.
- list_locations — List locations (facilities, terminals, yards) narrowed by status, code, name or city.
- list_location_categories — List location categories — how facilities are grouped, and what each offers: secure parking, overnight, a restroom, whether an appointment is required.
- create_location — Create a location record for a pickup or delivery address that has none, such as a facility read from a document.
- update_location — Change a location's name, description, address or category.
- update_location_status — Set one or more locations Active or Inactive, which decides whether stops can be booked at them.
- list_tractors — List tractors (power units) narrowed by status, ownership, or a registration or lease date.
- get_tractor — Retrieve one tractor by id, with its equipment details, fleet and assigned workers.
- locate_tractor — Record where a tractor actually is when it was moved outside a shipment, so dispatch plans from the right place.
- list_trailers — List trailers narrowed by status, ownership, or a registration, lease or inspection date.
- get_trailer — Retrieve one trailer by id, with its equipment details and fleet.
- update_trailer — Change a trailer: its equipment type, fleet, make, model, VIN, plate, registration, load limit or last inspection.
- locate_trailer — Record where a trailer actually is when it was moved outside a shipment.
- list_equipment_types — List equipment types — the trailer and tractor classes this organization books against, such as dry van, reefer or flatbed.
- list_equipment_manufacturers — List equipment manufacturers — who built the tractors and trailers in the fleet, such as Freightliner or Utility.
- list_fleet_codes — List fleet codes — the groupings drivers and equipment are assigned to, each with its own manager and revenue goal.
- search_shipments — List shipments, optionally narrowed by free text such as a pro number, BOL, customer name, or city, and by status.
- search_documents — Search the text of documents: rate confirmations, bills of lading, proofs of delivery, invoices, contracts, permits and other files attached to records.
- list_document_types — List the document types this organization files — rate confirmations, bills of lading, proofs of delivery and the rest.
- delete_documents — Delete documents that should not be on file, such as a duplicate upload or a scan of the wrong paperwork.
- restore_document_version — Make an earlier version of a document the current one again, when the newest upload was the wrong file.
- list_capture_batches — List scanned and printed paperwork waiting in capture intake, newest first.
- file_capture_items — File scanned documents from capture intake onto the shipment, worker, tractor, trailer, customer or carrier they belong to, as the document type they are.
- discard_capture_item — Throw away one scanned document from capture intake without filing it, such as a blank sheet, a duplicate or a stray page.
- discard_capture_batch — Throw away every unfiled document of a scanned stack in capture intake, when nothing left in it is worth filing.
- list_table_change_alerts — List the change alerts the person you are working for has set up: what each watches, for which changes, and whether it is Active or Paused.
- create_table_change_alert — Be told when a record changes in a particular way: a shipment reaching Delayed, a customer's credit hold coming on, a rate agreement's expiry being set.
- update_table_change_alert — Change one of the person's change alerts: what it watches, which changes, the conditions or its message.
- set_table_change_alert_status — Pause one of the person's change alerts so it stops notifying them, or resume a paused one.
- delete_table_change_alert — Delete one of the person's change alerts they no longer want.
